  "environment": "Linux container limited to 4 CPU / 8 GiB on a shared Docker Desktop host; Windows workspace bind mount; storage type not verified.",
  "workload": "Each size: 20 queries, each repeated 20 times with concurrency 5; plus 20 first executions, 20 warm-ups and one high-frequency gap 0..8.",
  "data_recipe": "s0-synthetic-v1 seed 20261016; 20 repeated templates of 100 whitespace tokens; one revision=document=sentence. This does not model natural corpus diversity.",
  "coordinate_method": "Every hit reads persisted token-to-Unicode-codepoint coordinates. All hits are mapped and counted before selecting 50 ordered KWIC rows from actual persisted text.",
  "independent_count_method": "Brute-force raw token matching for all 20 templates weighted by documented full/partial repetition, without CQP or PositionIndex; portable tests compare this weighting against full enumeration.",
  "timing_scope": [
    "First executions do not represent cold disk: OS page cache was not evicted.",
    "Every call launches a fresh CQP subprocess. Its startup, full span output and pipe backpressure are included in raw child wall time; this is not index-only query execution.",
    "Adapter wall time includes the raw child plus wrapper startup, stdout capture, parsing and deduplication. It overlaps the raw metric and must not be added to it.",
    "Full mapping/KWIC wall time is subsequent to the adapter stage; both are included in end-to-end first-page-and-complete-count time. Concurrent wall times include scheduling and Python GIL contention.",
    "Child CPU and peak RSS come from resource.getrusage in a fresh wrapper, while cgroup memory includes page cache. Disk peak is sampled every 0.25s, not an absolute peak."
  ],
  "acceptance_scope": "Exploratory candidate adapter only, not a deployed business API. The 3s first-page and 120s complete high-frequency count thresholds remain unchanged. Shared 4CPU/8GiB measurements do not satisfy dedicated 8-vCPU/32-GiB formal acceptance.",
